    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1045">

                <pb facs="0941" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9178a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-12T00:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                        1913—midnight</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>See the Minister for Foreign Affairs immediately and have him communicate to
                    Huerta the following:</p>
                <p>Any violence done to legislators will shock the civilized world and raise serious
                    questions with our own and other Governments. <pb facs="0942" n="838"
                        xml:id="pg838"/> The United States, as a neighboring nation, could not be
                    indifferent to the political execution of officials. Government, to be deserving
                    of respect, must conform to established laws and usage, and these require a fair
                    and full hearing of all charges before punishment can be legally inflicted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
